{"id":"p16-l14","minutes":40,"summary":"A planned path is only useful if the robot can follow it. Pure pursuit steers a wheeled robot by repeatedly driving the arc that reaches a point a fixed lookahead distance ahead on the path. You derive the curvature 2y/L² of that arc, implement pure pursuit for a differential-drive robot, and test that it tracks a circle exactly, converges from an offset, and keeps the cross-track error on a stadium-shaped track within a 5 cm spec, then see how steering lag calls for a longer lookahead.","html":"<h2 id=\"chase-a-point-ahead\">Chase a point ahead</h2>\n<p>Pick the point on the path a distance <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span> (the <strong>lookahead</strong>) ahead of the robot. In the robot’s frame, with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span></span></span> forward and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span></span></span> to the left, it is at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0085em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. Find the circular arc that starts at the robot, tangent to its heading, and passes through that point.</p>\n<p>The arc’s centre is on the robot’s <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span></span></span> axis at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>. The goal point is on the circle: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0085em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span></span></span></span>, and</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">κ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.0074em;vertical-align:-0.686em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3214em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.686em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.0074em;vertical-align:-0.686em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3214em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7401em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.989em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.686em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>Command the turn rate <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">κ</span></span></span></span> (the unicycle model of Phase 15) and repeat every control cycle with a new goal point.</p>\n<h2 id=\"choosing-the-lookahead\">Choosing the lookahead</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A <strong>circle</strong> is tracked exactly from any point on it, for any <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span> shorter than its diameter: a chord of a circle, with the robot tangent to it, defines an arc of the same circle.</li>\n<li>Where the curvature changes, such as where a straight meets a curve, the robot starts turning early and <strong>cuts the corner</strong>. The error grows with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>A short <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span> reacts sharply. If the steering responds with a lag, or the robot moves fast, a short lookahead overcorrects and the robot weaves. A longer <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span> damps it.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>So <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span> trades accuracy on curves against stability. Many implementations scale it with speed: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">max</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">min</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"purepursuit\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>A differential-drive robot following a stadium track with pure pursuit. The circle is the lookahead distance and the dot is the goal point. Lengthen the lookahead to see it cut corners, shorten it and add steering lag to see it weave.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>An illustrative robot at 0.5 m/s, turn rate limited to 3 rad/s, integrated with exact arcs every 10 ms.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>A circle of radius 2 m with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.6</span></span></span></span> m: the largest cross-track error is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">6</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">7</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> m, the sag of the 4000-point polyline the track is stored as.</li>\n<li>Starting 0.5 m outside that circle: after 10 s the error is 0.02 mm.</li>\n<li>A stadium track (4 m straights, 1.5 m radius ends), after the first 5 s: the largest error is 0.6 cm with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.3</span></span></span></span> m, 2.5 cm with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.6</span></span></span></span> m, and 10.9 cm with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.2</span></span></span></span> m. Against an illustrative 5 cm spec, 0.3 and 0.6 m pass and 1.2 m fails.</li>\n<li>With a 0.5 s first-order lag on the turn rate: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.15</span></span></span></span> m weaves, with errors up to 58.6 cm, while <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.6</span></span></span></span> m stays within 1.5 cm.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">purepursuit.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">stadium</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">straight=<span class=\"hljs-number\">4.0</span>, R=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.5</span>, n=<span class=\"hljs-number\">4000</span></span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;an illustrative closed track: two straights joined by semicircles, as a dense polyline (counter-clockwise)&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    u = np.linspace(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, n, endpoint=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">False</span>) * (<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * straight + <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi * R); pts = []\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> d <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> u:\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> d &lt; straight: pts.append((d - straight / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, -R))\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">elif</span> d &lt; straight + np.pi * R: a = -np.pi / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> + (d - straight) / R; pts.append((straight / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> + R * np.cos(a), R * np.sin(a)))\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">elif</span> d &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * straight + np.pi * R: pts.append((straight / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> - (d - straight - np.pi * R), R))\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span>: a = np.pi / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> + (d - <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * straight - np.pi * R) / R; pts.append((-straight / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> + R * np.cos(a), R * np.sin(a)))\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.array(pts)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">circle</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">R=<span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span>, n=<span class=\"hljs-number\">4000</span></span>):\n    a = np.linspace(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi, n, endpoint=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">False</span>); <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.stack([R * np.cos(a), R * np.sin(a)], <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">curvature_to</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">goal, pose</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;pure pursuit: the arc through the robot and the goal point, tangent to the heading, has curvature 2 y / L^2&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    x, y, th = pose; dx, dy = goal[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>] - x, goal[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] - y\n    yl = -np.sin(th) * dx + np.cos(th) * dy                  <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># lateral offset of the goal point in the robot frame</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * yl / (dx * dx + dy * dy)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">lookahead_point</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">track, pos, L, i0</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;first track point at least L ahead of the robot, searching forward from the closest point near the last index&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    n = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(track); idx = (i0 + np.arange(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">400</span>)) % n\n    i = idx[np.argmin(np.linalg.norm(track[idx] - pos, axis=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>))]\n    j = i\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">while</span> np.linalg.norm(track[(j + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) % n] - pos) &lt; L: j += <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>\n    a, b = track[j % n], track[(j + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) % n]                  <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># the exact point at distance L on segment a-b</span>\n    d, f = b - a, a - pos; A_, B_, C_ = d @ d, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * f @ d, f @ f - L * L\n    t = (-B_ + np.sqrt(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(B_ * B_ - <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span> * A_ * C_, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>))) / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * A_)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> a + np.clip(t, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) * d, i\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">cross_track</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">track, pos</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;distance to the nearest segment of the polyline&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    a, b = track, np.roll(track, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, axis=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>); d = b - a\n    t = np.clip(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>((pos - a) * d, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) / np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(d * d, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>), <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>(np.linalg.norm(a + t[:, <span class=\"hljs-literal\">None</span>] * d - pos, axis=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>))\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">run</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">track, L, v=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>, T=<span class=\"hljs-number\">40.0</span>, dt=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.01</span>, pose=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">None</span>, lag=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>, wmax=<span class=\"hljs-number\">3.0</span></span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;unicycle at speed v; the turn rate follows the commanded v * kappa through a first-order lag and a limit&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    p = np.array(pose <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> pose <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">is</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> <span class=\"hljs-literal\">None</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> [track[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>], track[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>], np.arctan2(*(track[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] - track[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>])[::-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>])], <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">float</span>)\n    w = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>; i = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; cte = []\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> k <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(T / dt)):\n        g, i = lookahead_point(track, p[:<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>], L, i)\n        wc = np.clip(v * curvature_to(g, p), -wmax, wmax)\n        w = wc <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> lag == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> w + dt / lag * (wc - w)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(w) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span>: p += [v * dt * np.cos(p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>]), v * dt * np.sin(p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>]), <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>]          <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># exact arc for constant v, w over dt</span>\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span>: p += [v / w * (np.sin(p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>] + w * dt) - np.sin(p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>])), -v / w * (np.cos(p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>] + w * dt) - np.cos(p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>])), w * dt]\n        cte.append(cross_track(track, p[:<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>]))\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.array(cte)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_circle_tracked_exactly</span>():\n    c = run(circle(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span>), L=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span>, pose=[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>, np.pi / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>], T=<span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;circle of radius 2 m: largest cross-track error <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{c.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>():<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>e}</span> m (any chord of a circle subtends an arc of that circle)&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> c.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-5</span>                                    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># what is left is the polyline sagging between its points</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_converges_from_offset</span>():\n    c = run(circle(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span>), L=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span>, pose=[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2.5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>, np.pi / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>], T=<span class=\"hljs-number\">30</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;start 0.5 m outside the circle: error <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{c[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.3</span>f}</span> m, after 10 s <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{c[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>] * <span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> mm, after 30 s <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{c[-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>e}</span> m&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> c[-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-5</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_stadium_within_spec</span>():\n    tr = stadium(); spec = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.05</span>                                <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># illustrative spec: 5 cm</span>\n    res = {L: run(tr, L, T=<span class=\"hljs-number\">45</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> L <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> (<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.3</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.2</span>)}\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> L, c <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> res.items(): <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;stadium, lookahead <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{L}</span> m: largest cross-track error after the first 5 s <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{c[<span class=\"hljs-number\">500</span>:].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() * <span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> cm&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> res[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.3</span>][<span class=\"hljs-number\">500</span>:].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() &lt; spec <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> res[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.2</span>][<span class=\"hljs-number\">500</span>:].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() &gt; res[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.3</span>][<span class=\"hljs-number\">500</span>:].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>()   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># longer lookahead cuts corners more</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_lag_needs_longer_lookahead</span>():\n    tr = stadium()\n    short, long_ = run(tr, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.15</span>, T=<span class=\"hljs-number\">45</span>, lag=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>), run(tr, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span>, T=<span class=\"hljs-number\">45</span>, lag=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;with a 0.5 s steering lag: lookahead 0.15 m error up to <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{short[<span class=\"hljs-number\">500</span>:].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() * <span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> cm, 0.6 m up to <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{long_[<span class=\"hljs-number\">500</span>:].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() * <span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> cm&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> short[<span class=\"hljs-number\">500</span>:].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() &gt; long_[<span class=\"hljs-number\">500</span>:].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>()\n\ntest_circle_tracked_exactly()\ntest_converges_from_offset()\ntest_stadium_within_spec()\ntest_lag_needs_longer_lookahead()\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"in-practice\">In practice</h2>\n<p>Nav2’s Regulated Pure Pursuit controller adds speed regulation on tight curves and near obstacles to this law. Pure pursuit goes back to path-tracking work for autonomous vehicles at Carnegie Mellon in the 1980s.</p>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>The goal point is at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0.4</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.3</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> in the robot frame. What are <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">κ</span></span></span></span> and the turning radius?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.5</span></span></span></span> m, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">κ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.3/0.25</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.4</span></span></span></span> 1/m, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.417</span></span></span></span> m, to the left.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why can’t pure pursuit follow a path with a sharp 90° corner exactly?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>It always drives arcs and starts turning once the goal point is round the corner, a distance <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span> early, so it cuts inside. A differential-drive robot could stop and turn on the spot, but pure pursuit’s continuous arcs never do. Smooth the path first (lesson 05), or shrink <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span> near corners.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p16-l14\"></div>\n","toc":[{"id":"chase-a-point-ahead","title":"Chase a point ahead"},{"id":"choosing-the-lookahead","title":"Choosing the lookahead"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"in-practice","title":"In practice"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p16-l14-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Curvature to a goal point with lateral offset y = 0.1 m and L = 0.5 m?</p>\n","explain":"<p>2y/L².</p>\n","answer":0.8,"tol":0.001,"unit":"1/m"},{"id":"p16-l14-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Turn rate at 0.5 m/s for that curvature?</p>\n","explain":"<p>ω = vκ.</p>\n","answer":0.4,"tol":0.001,"unit":"rad/s"},{"id":"p16-l14-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Turning radius for κ = 0.8 1/m?</p>\n","explain":"<p>R = 1/κ.</p>\n","answer":1.25,"tol":0.001,"unit":"m"},{"id":"p16-l14-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Curvature when the goal point is straight ahead (y = 0)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Drive straight.</p>\n","answer":0,"tol":0.001,"unit":"1/m"},{"id":"p16-l14-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>A longer lookahead distance…</p>\n","explain":"<p>It trades accuracy on curves for stability.</p>\n","options":["makes the robot weave","has no effect on a circle smaller than L","cuts corners more but steers more calmly","always reduces the cross-track error"],"answer":2},{"id":"p16-l14-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Pure pursuit tracks a circle exactly because…</p>\n","explain":"<p>A chord and a tangent define the circle uniquely.</p>\n","options":["the cross-track error is fed back","the lookahead is zero","the arc through the robot and a goal point on the circle, tangent to the circle, is the circle","the robot slows down on curves"],"answer":2}],"code":[{"file":"purepursuit.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\ndef stadium(straight=4.0, R=1.5, n=4000):\n    \"\"\"an illustrative closed track: two straights joined by semicircles, as a dense polyline (counter-clockwise)\"\"\"\n    u = np.linspace(0, 1, n, endpoint=False) * (2 * straight + 2 * np.pi * R); pts = []\n    for d in u:\n        if d < straight: pts.append((d - straight / 2, -R))\n        elif d < straight + np.pi * R: a = -np.pi / 2 + (d - straight) / R; pts.append((straight / 2 + R * np.cos(a), R * np.sin(a)))\n        elif d < 2 * straight + np.pi * R: pts.append((straight / 2 - (d - straight - np.pi * R), R))\n        else: a = np.pi / 2 + (d - 2 * straight - np.pi * R) / R; pts.append((-straight / 2 + R * np.cos(a), R * np.sin(a)))\n    return np.array(pts)\n\ndef circle(R=2.0, n=4000):\n    a = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, n, endpoint=False); return np.stack([R * np.cos(a), R * np.sin(a)], 1)\n\ndef curvature_to(goal, pose):\n    \"\"\"pure pursuit: the arc through the robot and the goal point, tangent to the heading, has curvature 2 y / L^2\"\"\"\n    x, y, th = pose; dx, dy = goal[0] - x, goal[1] - y\n    yl = -np.sin(th) * dx + np.cos(th) * dy                  # lateral offset of the goal point in the robot frame\n    return 2 * yl / (dx * dx + dy * dy)\n\ndef lookahead_point(track, pos, L, i0):\n    \"\"\"first track point at least L ahead of the robot, searching forward from the closest point near the last index\"\"\"\n    n = len(track); idx = (i0 + np.arange(-50, 400)) % n\n    i = idx[np.argmin(np.linalg.norm(track[idx] - pos, axis=1))]\n    j = i\n    while np.linalg.norm(track[(j + 1) % n] - pos) < L: j += 1\n    a, b = track[j % n], track[(j + 1) % n]                  # the exact point at distance L on segment a-b\n    d, f = b - a, a - pos; A_, B_, C_ = d @ d, 2 * f @ d, f @ f - L * L\n    t = (-B_ + np.sqrt(max(B_ * B_ - 4 * A_ * C_, 0.0))) / (2 * A_)\n    return a + np.clip(t, 0, 1) * d, i\n\ndef cross_track(track, pos):\n    \"\"\"distance to the nearest segment of the polyline\"\"\"\n    a, b = track, np.roll(track, -1, axis=0); d = b - a\n    t = np.clip(np.sum((pos - a) * d, 1) / np.sum(d * d, 1), 0, 1)\n    return np.min(np.linalg.norm(a + t[:, None] * d - pos, axis=1))\n\ndef run(track, L, v=0.5, T=40.0, dt=0.01, pose=None, lag=0.0, wmax=3.0):\n    \"\"\"unicycle at speed v; the turn rate follows the commanded v * kappa through a first-order lag and a limit\"\"\"\n    p = np.array(pose if pose is not None else [track[0, 0], track[0, 1], np.arctan2(*(track[1] - track[0])[::-1])], float)\n    w = 0.0; i = 0; cte = []\n    for k in range(int(T / dt)):\n        g, i = lookahead_point(track, p[:2], L, i)\n        wc = np.clip(v * curvature_to(g, p), -wmax, wmax)\n        w = wc if lag == 0 else w + dt / lag * (wc - w)\n        if abs(w) < 1e-9: p += [v * dt * np.cos(p[2]), v * dt * np.sin(p[2]), 0.0]          # exact arc for constant v, w over dt\n        else: p += [v / w * (np.sin(p[2] + w * dt) - np.sin(p[2])), -v / w * (np.cos(p[2] + w * dt) - np.cos(p[2])), w * dt]\n        cte.append(cross_track(track, p[:2]))\n    return np.array(cte)\n\ndef test_circle_tracked_exactly():\n    c = run(circle(2.0), L=0.6, pose=[2.0, 0.0, np.pi / 2], T=20)\n    print(f\"circle of radius 2 m: largest cross-track error {c.max():.1e} m (any chord of a circle subtends an arc of that circle)\")\n    assert c.max() < 1e-5                                    # what is left is the polyline sagging between its points\n\ndef test_converges_from_offset():\n    c = run(circle(2.0), L=0.6, pose=[2.5, 0.0, np.pi / 2], T=30)\n    print(f\"start 0.5 m outside the circle: error {c[0]:.3f} m, after 10 s {c[1000] * 1000:.2f} mm, after 30 s {c[-1]:.1e} m\")\n    assert c[-1] < 1e-5\n\ndef test_stadium_within_spec():\n    tr = stadium(); spec = 0.05                                # illustrative spec: 5 cm\n    res = {L: run(tr, L, T=45) for L in (0.3, 0.6, 1.2)}\n    for L, c in res.items(): print(f\"stadium, lookahead {L} m: largest cross-track error after the first 5 s {c[500:].max() * 100:.1f} cm\")\n    assert res[0.3][500:].max() < spec and res[1.2][500:].max() > res[0.3][500:].max()   # longer lookahead cuts corners more\n\ndef test_lag_needs_longer_lookahead():\n    tr = stadium()\n    short, long_ = run(tr, 0.15, T=45, lag=0.5), run(tr, 0.6, T=45, lag=0.5)\n    print(f\"with a 0.5 s steering lag: lookahead 0.15 m error up to {short[500:].max() * 100:.1f} cm, 0.6 m up to {long_[500:].max() * 100:.1f} cm\")\n    assert short[500:].max() > long_[500:].max()\n\ntest_circle_tracked_exactly()\ntest_converges_from_offset()\ntest_stadium_within_spec()\ntest_lag_needs_longer_lookahead()\nprint(\"PASS\")"}]}